  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_coldst",
      "name": {
        "en": "Coldshot's Badge",
        "zh": "冰酿证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_coldst",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Coldshot has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for storing and unleashing capacitance-based firepower to penetrative ends when facing the enemy.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Hunter responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员冰酿擅长蓄积火力对敌人进行贯穿打击\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使猎手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_coldst",
      "name": {
        "en": "'Unbridled'",
        "zh": "“桀骜”",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_coldst",
      "description": {
        "en": "'What a fine beast.' When the ranch owner takes Helena to see the burdenbeast that evening, this is the first thought that crosses her mind.\nThe burdenbeast stands proud in the corral, its stocky build much larger than any burdenbeast Helena has ever tamed. Fresh scars mar its face and neck, while a fading name is branded onto the side of its belly by hot iron, making it seem particularly extraordinary.\nExtraordinary—an apt word to describe what the burdenbeast has endured. The ranch owner tells Helena that it took the hunters quite some effort to capture it. Tracking the beast alone took five days, as its tracks led them across mountains and valleys, through forests and creeks, almost straight into a full-on Catastrophe. Only after almost wearing out their boots and exhausting all their tranquilizer arrows did they finally manage to bring this legendary burdenbeast back. Many renowned riders have since tried to tame it, all to no avail.\n'What a fine beast,' Helena exclaims.\n'That's right. That's why you're our last hope at taming it,' the ranch owner responds, sounding slightly defeated. 'If even you can't tame it, I'll have no choice but to send it to the slaughterhouse.'\nHelena takes out the bridle and vaults over the fence.\nShe advances slowly and gently towards the burdenbeast until they are less than half a meter apart. In one hand, she holds the bridle; with the other, she caresses its face, fingers tracing the new and old scars. Before anyone can react, she slips the bridle over its neck, tightens the reins, and effortlessly flips onto the beast's back.\nThe ranch owner's gasp is instantly drowned out by the beast's deafening neighs. Helena quickly steadies herself, holding tightly onto the reins no matter how hard the beast kicks and shakes. Enraged, the beast rears up on its hind legs and lets out a furious cry. Helena leans forward, pressing her body entirely against its back. Despite all these years, even as its mane has hardened and its hide has grown rough, the vigor and life force of the wild still course through its veins.\nHelena recalls the evening of her seventeenth birthday. Her father had given her a burdenbeast as a present and had used a hot iron to brand its name onto the side of its belly. 'Anna.'\n'Anna. What a fine beast.' That was what Helena had thought.\nDiscreetly, Helena takes out a dagger from her pocket and, with a gentle nick, cuts the rein. With all its strength, 'Anna' shakes off the bridle and Helena. For a fleeting moment, Helena feels as if their gazes meet, though she cannot be sure. Half a second later, 'Anna' clears the fence with a single leap.\n'Holy! You nearly had it, Helena!' The ranch owner's tone is a mix of excitement and shame.\n'What a fine beast.' That's all Helena says as she gets back up, pats the dirt off herself, and watches as the burdenbeast gallops back into the wild.",
        "zh": "“真是个好苗子。”那天傍晚，牧场主第一次带海伦娜见到这匹驮兽，她心里这么想。\n这匹驮兽伫立在围栏之中，它体格健壮，个头也比海伦娜所驯服过的其他驮兽大得多。它的脸上、脖子上还有刚结痂的伤，侧腹有一行即将褪去的烙印，好像是一个名字，这让它看起来很不寻常。\n这匹驮兽的来历确实不寻常，据牧场主说，猎人们捕获它的时候费了好大的劲，光是追踪它就花了五天时间，它的踪迹带着猎人们穿过了高山深谷、溪流树林，还差点把猎人们引向一场飞沙走石的天灾。几乎是跨越了整个州，用完了所有的麻醉箭矢，猎人们才把这匹不凡的驮兽带回来。周边许多有名的骑手都尝试过驯服它，但无一例外，都败下阵来。\n“真是个好苗子。”海伦娜感叹道。\n“所以只能请你来驯了。”牧场主听起来无可奈何，“如果它还是不能乖乖听话，我就只能把它送去屠宰场了。”\n海伦娜早已准备好辔头，她二话不说，跨过围栏。\n海伦娜踱着步子，渐渐接近驮兽，直到她们之间的距离不足半米。海伦娜一手拿着辔头，一手轻轻拂过驮兽的脸庞，拂过那些新伤旧疤——仅在瞬间，她把辔头套上驮兽的脖颈，收紧皮革，翻身跃上这匹野兽。\n牧场主发出一声惊呼，但被驮兽的嘶鸣盖了过去。海伦娜迅速坐稳，任凭这匹野兽如何挣扎，她都死死拉着皮带。直到驮兽前蹄扬起，发出一声长啸，海伦娜附身，完全靠在了它的身上。这么多年过去了，即使鬃毛已经坚硬，皮肤已经粗糙，在那每一寸肌肤之下、每一缕血管之中依旧充满了活力，属于荒野的活力。\n海伦娜回想起十七岁生日时，她的父亲在这匹作为生日礼物的驮兽侧腹烙上“安娜”的那个傍晚。\n“‘安娜’，真是个好苗子。”海伦娜当时就这么想。\n海伦娜悄悄从口袋抽出匕首，轻轻一刀割断了皮带。“安娜”铆足力气，挣开皮带，也把她从身上甩了下来。海伦娜感觉她们的眼神似乎有了一瞬交会，似乎又没有。半秒钟后，“安娜”纵身一跃，跨出了围栏。\n“啊，啊！海伦娜，你果然有一套，差点就成了！”牧场主的语气中不乏惋惜。\n“真是个好苗子。”但海伦娜依旧这么说。她从地上爬了起来，掸了掸身上的泥土，然后默默看着驮兽重新奔向了荒野。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
